.TH GETPW 3 deprecated
.SH NAME
getpw \- get name from UID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int getpw(int uid, char *buf);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Getpw
searches the password file for
the (numerical)
.IR uid ", and fills in " "buf"
with the corresponding line;
it returns non-zero if
.IR uid ""
could not
be found.
The line is null-terminated.
.PP
.B Note:
it is declared at its own file head and by no header, which is this tree's rule
for a routine no v7 header names.  Prefer
.IR getpwuid (3),
which is what "deprecated" in the title has always meant here.
.SH FILES
/etc/passwd
.br
share/besm6/lib/libc.a, lib/libc/stdio/getpw.c
.SH "SEE ALSO"
getpwent(3),
passwd(5)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Non-zero
return on error.
.SH BUGS
.I Buf
must be large enough for a whole line of /etc/passwd and there is no way to say
how large it is.
.SH BESM-6 NOTES
One v7 bug is fixed rather than carried.  Two of the field walks were guarded
against a `\\n' that cannot be present, the line having been read a character at
a time and terminated already \- so
.B a line with fewer than three colons walked off the end of the caller's buffer.
Both walks stop at the terminator now.
